# {{.Name}}

Native sporemind plugin — three-layer unified scaffold.

## Three-Layer Model

This project uses the three-layer unified model:

1. **Definition** (`app.appdef`) — declarative app definition: callables,
   entrypoints, schemas. This is the single source of truth.
2. **Generation** (`main.gen.go`, `schemas_gen.go`, `app.manifest.json`,
   `client.gen.ts`, `handlers.go`) — produced by `codegen.Generate` from the
   `.appdef`. **Do not edit generated files** (except `handlers.go`).
3. **Implementation** (`handlers.go`) — the sole agent-owned file. Fill in
   callable handler bodies (replace `sdk.ErrNotImplemented` returns with real
   logic). Re-run generate after editing `app.appdef` to create new stubs.

## Build

	GOWORK=off go build -buildmode=c-shared -o app-{{.Name}}.dll .

## Structure

- `app.appdef` — declarative app definition (source of truth)
- `main.gen.go` — generated: plugin registration + C ABI exports
- `handlers.go` — generated stubs, then agent-owned (implement callables here)
- `schemas_gen.go` — generated: Go struct types from appdef
- `app.manifest.json` — generated: host manifest
- `client.gen.ts` — generated: TypeScript client types + invoke wrappers
- `go.mod` — module definition (replace points to vendored SDK)
- `vendor-sdk/` — minimal ABI layer (zero external dependencies)

## Workflow

1. Edit `app.appdef` to declare callables, entrypoints, and schemas.
2. Run `codegen.Generate` (or `appmanager.dev_generate`) to produce all
   generated files.
3. Fill in handler stubs in `handlers.go` (replace `sdk.ErrNotImplemented`).
4. Build with `GOWORK=off go build -buildmode=c-shared`.

## Upgrading to full SDK

To use host capabilities (LLM, project I/O, notifications), replace the
vendored SDK with the full SDK. Update `go.mod`:

	replace github.com/qomos-w/sporemind-plugin-sdk => ../../sporemind-plugin-sdk

Then use `ctx.Host()` in your OnLoad handler.
